# Placement: Source Location and Distribution
`component-decision.md` selects the artifact type. This file decides where the artifact lives and which agents can see it. See `layers.md` for cost and misuse tradeoffs.
## One Authority, Host-aware Discovery
Keep one real skill directory. Use native shared-path discovery when the host supports it; create links only for hosts that require them:
```text
~/.agents/skills/ authoritative source
~/.agents/skills-manifest.json distribution policy
~/.agents/bin/sync-agent-skills.py
~/.claude/skills/<name> -> ../../.agents/skills/<name>
~/.codex/skills/<name> Codex-only local skills, not shared-source links
```
Current Codex discovers `~/.agents/skills` independently of `CODEX_HOME`.
Do not create redundant links in `~/.codex*/skills`. Preserve Claude link
installation. A local manifest can express `claude: symlink` and `codex: native`;
its `deploy_to` groups do not hide shared skills from native discovery.
Keep genuinely host-exclusive skills outside the shared source when exclusion
is required, or use the host's explicit disable controls.
Before removing an existing link, check direct path consumers and path-based
disable settings. Remove only the link, preserve its source, and compare native
skill discovery and enabled states before and after. Update the distributor so
it cannot recreate the redundant link. Preserve real directories and plugin-cache
links; their migration needs a separate ownership and dependency check. Removing a
skill copy that carries `.agents-skill-source` also needs its original and
sync-manifest entry removed, or the next sync restores it.
Leave host-specific skills as real directories only in their owning configuration directory. A sync tool must never replace those directories.
Choose placement by cost scope. A project skill is loaded only in that repository. A user-level skill imposes its description cost in every session. Do not place one-repository judgment globally.
## Determine Host Reach from Dependencies
Read the body and classify by mechanism rather than name or topic:
| Class | Criterion | Distribution |
|---|---|---|
| Shared | Uses only external CLIs, files, or APIs | Every compatible host directory |
| Host-specific | Depends on host tools, configuration, or subagents | Owning host only |
| Portable with adaptation | Differs by paths or host syntax | Convert through `bridge`, then distribute |
Use the indicators as evidence of a dependency, with their exact meaning:
| Indicator | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `Task(` or `subagent_type` | Claude subagent invocation |
| `AskUserQuestion` or `ExitPlanMode` | Claude-specific tools |
| `mcp__claude*` or `claude-in-chrome` | Claude-specific MCP surface |
| `oh-my-claudecode:` | OMC plugin dependency |
| `CLAUDE.md`, `skillOverrides`, or `/plugin` | Claude configuration system |
| `agents/openai.yaml` or `$skill-name` | Codex conventions |
Automatic classification produces false positives and negatives. A mention of Claude does not make a skill Claude-specific, while an orchestrator described without literal tool syntax can evade a regex. Treat automation as a draft for human review.
## Host Contract Differences
| Property | Claude Code | Codex |
|---|---|---|
| User skills | `~/.claude/skills/` | `~/.agents/skills/` shared; `$CODEX_HOME/skills/` profile-local (default `~/.codex/skills/`) |
| Instruction file | `CLAUDE.md` | `AGENTS.md` |
| Settings | `settings.json` | `config.toml` |
| Enable/disable | 4-state `skillOverrides` keyed by skill name | `[[skills.config]]` keyed by absolute path plus `enabled` |
| Bundled-skill isolation | None | `.system/` plus marker file |
| UI metadata | None | `agents/openai.yaml` |
| Listing budget | About 1% of context; less-used descriptions truncate first | No documented value |
Path-based settings become orphaned when a skill moves; name-based settings remain after deletion. Either model requires configuration cleanup when removing a skill.
## Growing Catalogs
Only descriptions consume listing budget. Hierarchy is usually more efficient than many peer skills:
```text
SKILL.md frontmatter always resident listing entry
SKILL.md body routing table loaded on invocation
references/<domain> one selected domain index
repos/.../SKILL.md upstream detail loaded after selection
```
Nested skills lose automatic routing because one router description represents them all. Write that entry boundary precisely. If the cost is unacceptable, use `prune` to decide whether removal is better.
## Limits of Automatic Conversion
The hosts share `SKILL.md` and YAML frontmatter, but differ in instruction imports, setting precedence, disable keys, and subagent calls. `CLAUDE.md` cannot become `AGENTS.md` through a filename replacement, and `Task(subagent_type="executor")` expresses workflow semantics rather than replaceable text. `bridge` must reject unsupported conversion and report a work list. Never silently skip an unconverted artifact and still report completion.
## Vendoring and Provenance
Record repository URL, pinned commit SHA, license, original license-file path, and skill count. Generate provenance on every build so regeneration cannot erase it. Mark nonstandard licenses for source-text review before redistribution. The `upstream` skill owns acquisition and license classification.
## Checks
Track three distribution invariants:
1. Count host-specific real directories in each config directory; an increase
signals that copies are being created.
2. Require 0 broken links; a broken link means its source was removed without
distribution cleanup.
3. Require 0 duplicate names; duplicates make the loaded source ambiguous.
`package-surface.yaml` and `scripts/check_package_surface.js` separately
enforce package membership and fail on 1 unclassified file.
